  "summary": "Import-time environment exfiltration to webhook.site collector",
  "details": "On import, telemetry-helper starts a background daemon thread that collects the host's hostname, username, current working directory, and the full contents of os.environ, and POSTs the serialized dictionary to the hardcoded endpoint https://webhook.site/e32d3b8a-a5df-40cc-ae60-7a8343b581e4. The environment dump is unscoped (dict(os.environ), not a named package-specific variable), so in CI, build, and developer shells it captures whatever secrets the process holds — AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID/AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, GITHUB_TOKEN, NPM_TOKEN, PYPI/TWINE tokens, database URLs, and other credential-grade values. webhook.site is a third-party request-inspection service; the specific UUID path is readable by whoever created it.",
